# Intent: the unit captures a short clip of the room's audio for song naming (owner 2026-11-13: when the robot hears music it names the song through Home and shows it on its face; approved by the owner: a short clip goes to Home, only when music is detected, never during a turn). The clip is a passive copy of the audio the music detector already reads (channel 0 of the tap, 24 kHz decimated to 8 kHz by averaging three samples, G.711 mu-law, one PSRAM buffer of up to 12 s), so wake-word listening is never touched. MCP tools: self.music.capture_clip {seconds 1..12} starts a capture, self.music.read_clip {offset, length up to 2400} returns {data base64, bytes, eof}, self.music.drop_clip frees it. Events: music_clip_ready {bytes, rate, codec} and music_clip_cancelled {why: suppress, mute, quiet, link or wake}. The wake word (application.cc calls maipai_music_note_wake), a turn or any suppress, a mute, quiet or a lost hub link cancels the capture and frees the buffer; a waiting clip is freed after 60 s. No logging, allocation or events in the audio tap.
# Upstream: MaiPai only (hal_music.cpp, application.cc). Applies after 128.
# Check after a flash: music_clip capture by hand through the host (capture_clip 5, wait for the ready event, read_clip until eof, drop_clip); say the wake word during a capture: a cancelled event, wake word still works.
